Subject: [freebsd-ports PATCH 0/2] net-mgmt/signoz-otel-collector: New port
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:22:26 +0000

This packages the SigNoz OpenTelemetry Collector as its own port,
net-mgmt/signoz-otel-collector. SigNoz needs it twice over: it is the
only thing that writes telemetry to ClickHouse, and its "migrate"
subcommand creates the schema that SigNoz queries. The two packages
do not depend on each other, since the collector may run on another
host. The second patch makes net-mgmt/signoz name the collector's
origin.

The series applies on top of v10 of "[freebsd-ports PATCH v10]
net-mgmt/signoz: Observability platform for logs, metrics, and
traces" [1], which is not yet in the ports tree. That patch adds the
signoz user and group (UID and GID 485) that the collector shares, and
the port that the second patch edits.

Notes for review:

Checked: makesum, a clean extract and patch (sonic is swapped for the
v1.15.4 tuple, bf12ab8 applies to it, and both _freebsd.go copies are
in place), portclippy, portfmt, and portlint, all clean, and sh -n on
the rc script. Not checked: a build, the plist, a run from rc.d, the
migrations, OpAMP, or aarch64. The fixes are the three that let the
collector build and run "--help" on this host when I built it by hand
for the research reply [2]. The plist is drafted from post-install.

Version: v0.144.14, the latest release (2026-10-13). Nothing pins a
collector version to signoz v0.145.0; upstream's own CI and examples
use a range of v0.142 to v0.144 releases. The license is AGPLv3, not
Apache 2.0 like the upstream OpenTelemetry Collector.

Build fixes. The collector pins the same sonic v1.14.1 as signoz, so
it takes the same GH_TUPLE swap to v1.15.4 and the same post-patch
application of sonic commit bf12ab8, both copied from net-mgmt/signoz.
Two vendored packages have no FreeBSD code:

- opentelemetry-collector-contrib receiver/filestatsreceiver v0.144.0
  has its BSD code in filestats_darwin.go. The build line names
  freebsd, but the _darwin suffix restricts the file to darwin, so the
  build fails with "undefined: collectStats". Upstream issue 42645
  reports it, and PR 45680 renames the file to filestats_bsd.go, in a
  contrib release later than the one the collector pins. post-patch
  copies it to filestats_freebsd.go.
- github.com/AthenZ/athenz libs/go/sia/util v1.12.13, pulled in by the
  Pulsar exporter, has Linux, darwin, and windows files only.
  post-patch copies os_util_linux.go to os_util_freebsd.go, exactly as
  net/redpanda-connect does for the same package. The Linux and darwin
  files differ in one log message.

dns/zdns and devel/pinact copy a vendored _linux.go file to
_freebsd.go the same way.

Only cmd/signozotelcollector is built. cmd/signozschemamigrator is the
older standalone migrator, superseded by "signoz-otel-collector
migrate", which upstream's Linux install guide uses instead.

User. The collector runs as the signoz user, as both upstream's Linux
install guide and its Foundry systemd units do. USERS=signoz in both
ports is the tree's usual way to share a user; prometheus is shared by
six ports this way. Its state lives in /var/db/signoz-otel-collector.

Configuration. Upstream's conf/default.yaml is a development config: it
mixes tcp://localhost:9000 and tcp://clickhouse:9000, has no logs
pipeline, and scrapes host metrics. The port installs instead the config
from upstream's Linux install guide [3], verbatim apart from a header
comment, as files/config.yaml, like net/redpanda-connect's. It becomes
/usr/local/etc/signoz-otel-collector/config.yaml.sample.
conf/manager.yaml, the OpAMP config pointing at
ws://127.0.0.1:4320/v1/opamp, is installed as opamp.yaml.sample.

With --manager-config the collector does not run config.yaml as it
stands. It copies it to --copy-path, starts with every pipeline's
receivers and exporters replaced by nop, and runs the configuration
SigNoz sends over OpAMP, writing it to that copy (and a .rollback
beside it). That is what upstream deploys, so it is the rc.d default,
and pkg-message says the collector ingests nothing until SigNoz
answers. signoz_otel_collector_manager_config="" runs config.yaml
unmanaged. --copy-path defaults upstream to
/etc/otel/signozcol-config.yaml; rc.d sets
/var/db/signoz-otel-collector/config.yaml, which the signoz user can
write.

rc.d follows net-mgmt/signoz's script, itself from
net-mgmt/prometheus3: daemon(8) as the signoz user, with start_precmd
creating the pidfile. It adds an extra command, "service
signoz_otel_collector migrate", which runs as the signoz user the four
steps of the install guide: migrate ready, bootstrap, sync up, and
async up. The DSN comes from signoz_otel_collector_clickhouse_dsn,
since the migrations read it from --clickhouse-dsn, while the
collector itself reads the DSNs in its config. Other flags, such as
SIGNOZ_OTEL_COLLECTOR_CLICKHOUSE_REPLICATION=false, go in
signoz_otel_collector_env. start does not run "migrate sync check"
first, as Foundry's unit does, because rc.d has no restart to retry
it while ClickHouse is still starting.

Tests are not hooked up; upstream's need a ClickHouse server.

